      "body": "## Motivation\n\nPi0.5 masked attention currently uses PyTorch SDPA in `LocalAttention`. On Ascend, representative isolated tests indicate that fused infer attention can be faster for the tested shapes. This draft explores routing a restricted NPU case to FIA.\n\nRelated to #47834.\n\n## Prototype\n\n- Gate the experimental path behind `SGLANG_EXPERIMENTAL_NPU_FIA_MASKED_ATTENTION=1`; the existing path remains the default.\n- For 4D floating-point masks, check for zero and dtype-min-range values and fall back to SDPA for other values or fully masked rows.\n- Convert the mask to the operator's skip-mask convention. Do not cache the decision on mutable tensors.\n\n**Not ready for merge:** the threshold does not establish mask provenance or semantics for all callers. Maintainer feedback on carrying an explicitly typed/known pi0.5 mask through the attention interface would be welcome. The per-call checks can synchronize the device and must be evaluated for overhead.\n\n## Evidence and validation\n\nPrior 910C isolated microbenchmarks reported approximately 3x at BS=1 and 5.9x at BS=32 for FIA plus mask conversion versus SDPA. A separate same-node open-loop comparison using identical arrival-trace hashes observed lower FIA latency, but ran each variant once sequentially; repeat/alternating runs remain necessary. **Those results used a different, cached experimental patch; they are not measurements of the prototype in this PR, which deliberately avoids caching. No end-to-end performance claim is made for this implementation.**\n\n- [x] Python syntax parsed locally.\n- [ ] Verify mask polarity, finite additive-bias handling, fully masked rows, supported layouts and dtypes on Ascend.\n- [ ] Add tests covering dispatch, fallback, and mutation; compare full pi0.5 action outputs with fixed inputs.\n- [ ] Verify actual FIA dispatch and perform matched same-node repeated performance tests on this exact code.\n- [ ] Run appropriate upstream tests and CI.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41415449935](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41415449935)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41415449880](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41415449880)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #41415449901](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41415449901)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
